# 👀 Step 1 — Open the Challenge Page

Open the challenge URL.

You'll see a textbox containing JavaScript code similar to:

```javascript
javascript:(function() {
    var encryptedFlag = "àÒÆÞ¦È¬ëÙ£Ö...";
    var key = "picoctf";
    var decryptedFlag = "";

    for (var i = 0; i < encryptedFlag.length; i++) {
        decryptedFlag += String.fromCharCode(
            (encryptedFlag.charCodeAt(i) -
             key.charCodeAt(i % key.length) + 256) % 256
        );
    }

    alert(decryptedFlag);
})();
```

The exact encrypted string may differ depending on the challenge instance.

---

## 🔍 Understanding the Code

| Code                    | Purpose                                          |
| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |
| `encryptedFlag`         | Contains the scrambled flag 🔒                   |
| `key`                   | Key used to decrypt the flag 🔑                  |
| `for` loop              | Processes every character                        |
| `charCodeAt()`          | Converts characters into numeric character codes |
| `String.fromCharCode()` | Converts numbers back into characters            |
| `alert()`               | Displays the decrypted flag 🎉                   |

### 🧠 In Simple Terms

The code performs:

```text
Encrypted Flag
      ↓
Character-by-character calculation
      ↓
Decryption
      ↓
Decrypted Flag
      ↓
alert()
      ↓
🏆 Flag
```

The important point is that **both the encrypted data and the decryption logic are already available to us**.

