---

## 🔐 Key Takeaway

> **Client-side code is visible and controllable by the user.**

The challenge demonstrates why simply encrypting or obfuscating a secret on the client doesn't make it secure when the **key and decryption logic are also delivered to the client**.

### 🎓 Remember

* 🔖 **Bookmarklet** = A bookmark that executes JavaScript.
* 🌐 **DevTools** = Browser tools for inspecting and interacting with webpages.
* 💻 **Console** = Allows JavaScript to be executed in the browser.
* 🔑 **Client-side encryption** ≠ secure secret storage when the key is also exposed.
* 🛡️ **Never send sensitive secrets to an untrusted client.**
